# Which reasons each question has taken, as a three-letter word. One row per question: the mask
# reads `n u a` for none, unmeasured and notApplicable, with a dot where no loaded document has
# used that reason.
#
# The reasons a question has taken, as one word
#   There are three reasons, so the ones a question has taken make a word rather than a list.
#   Asked as rows, "which reasons does `remainder sign` file" is a pile of rows nobody reads. Asked
#   as a word, it reads like `.ua`, and it sits beside `boundOrigin`'s `nua` in a sorted column
#   where the missing letter is the first thing the eye lands on.
#
# A reason allowed and never taken is a question
#   Sometimes it is a defect: the type allows a reason that its own annotation refuses in prose.
#   The mask sets what was taken beside what the type allows. A word in a sorted column is a
#   comparison a reader makes at a glance; a pile of annotations is not.
#
# The masks cluster
#   Sort by the word and the wrappers fall into a handful of kinds. Two questions with one mask are
#   the same kind of question; a mask that takes fewer reasons than another is a candidate for the
#   narrower type. It is a candidate and never a verdict: a site may simply be young. The reading is
#   "go and look at this one", which is what an observation is for.
#
# It does not know what is allowed
#   It knows only what was taken. What is allowed lives in the XSD (`pm:Absence` is `nua`,
#   `pm:ClaimAbsence` is `.ua`) and in this database as the `a_..._absence_has_no_none` CHECKs.
#   Comparing the two is the reader's job, and saying so plainly is better than a relation that
#   guesses at a grammar it cannot see.
#
# A derivation is not a letter
#   It is not a blank: it names the identity that works out the position, and
#   epistemics/derivations.sqlc counts it.
-- epistemics/absences.sqlc folded to one three-letter word per question.
SELECT a.question,
       (CASE WHEN bool_or(a.reason = 'none')          THEN 'n' ELSE '.' END) ||
       (CASE WHEN bool_or(a.reason = 'unmeasured')    THEN 'u' ELSE '.' END) ||
       (CASE WHEN bool_or(a.reason = 'notApplicable') THEN 'a' ELSE '.' END) AS mask,
       count(*)                                                             AS filings,
       count(*) FILTER (WHERE a.reason = 'none')                            AS as_none
FROM (
    :compose(epistemics/absences.sqlc)
) a
WHERE a.reason IS NOT NULL
GROUP BY a.question
